true] [17592186279127 1113 #uuid "4988074d-c4b5-57bf-b07b-239bfc1142f9" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279127 1145 "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=12{t}^{4},$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{2}-10)=2t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(12{t}^{4})}{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{48{t}^{3}}{2t} \\\\  & =24{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=1,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{t=1}=24\\cdot {1}^{2}=24.\n$$" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279129 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279130 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279131 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279132 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279133 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1041 "selection" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279133 13194139534154 true] [17592186279128 1110 #uuid "b5ca8fcf-6954-5dc4-8321-2b71977f0a6e" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279129 1034 "12" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279129 1111 #uuid "f56c59dd-a88d-5cdb-b9c0-bb7579bcf5cb" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279130 1034 "9" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279130 1111 #uuid "afeb38fc-d951-5c91-a424-50cffbea441c" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279131 1034 "3" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279131 1111 #uuid "ba44c410-f3a5-543f-a69a-8d739070e7d6" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279132 1034 "6" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279132 1111 #uuid "06984140-0656-57c2-8cea-326938b0c014" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279133 1034 "24" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279133 1111 #uuid "a529b13a-d8f6-5a50-80f9-b9e40acf38bb" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279134 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279135 13194139534154 true] [17592186279134 1089 "q-352392" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279134 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534154 true] [17592186279134 1100 "A curve has parametric equations $x={e}^{2t},\\,y={e}^{6t}.$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{4t},$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,1}=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279134 1113 #uuid "f23207c5-dc3b-502d-9895-716f52882c8a" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279134 1145 "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3{e}^{4t},$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}({e}^{2t})=2{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(3{e}^{4t})}{2{e}^{2t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{e}^{4t}}{2{e}^{2t}} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=1,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,1}=6{e}^{2(1)}=6{e}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279136 13194139534154 true] [17592186279135 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534154 true] [17592186279135 1041 "field-1" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279135 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279136 13194139534154 true] [17592186279135 1110 #uuid "9cfa5fd6-e542-5ee3-a18e-d3564431c796" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279136 1034 "6e^{2}" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279136 1111 #uuid "cc8fb99d-5637-5eec-8c53-c9cad261ff6d" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279137 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279138 13194139534154 true] [17592186279137 1089 "q-78951" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279137 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534154 true] [17592186279137 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1.$ Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279137 1113 #uuid "0e2cd58a-0e3a-5779-a922-6155d814596a" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279137 1145 "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2{csc}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{3}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279139 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279140 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279141 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279142 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279143 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1041 "selection" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279142 13194139534154 true] [17592186279138 1110 #uuid "685815d1-1ed0-59c7-8ae3-f8a94d16c816" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279139 1034 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279139 1111 #uuid "b61d4ec9-d636-575f-839d-fb57453e40f3" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279140 1034 "-2{csc}^{2}⁡t" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279140 1111 #uuid "5f9a464b-1d2d-5e21-a52a-9403e0a68967" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279141 1034 "{sec}^{3}⁡t" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279141 1111 #uuid "82f1333c-b8da-52c3-8a7b-8951e9938b3a" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279142 1034 "-2{csc}^{3}⁡t" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279142 1111 #uuid "1f22d3a9-5228-5c1a-8a86-52ac286eb952" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279143 1034 "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279143 1111 #uuid "7ef6a1ce-d92a-55ba-a777-e2106002860e" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279144 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279145 13194139534154 true] [17592186279144 1089 "q-78959" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279144 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534154 true] [17592186279144 1100 "A curve has parametric equations $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+4,\\,y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t),$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{9}.$" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279144 1113 #uuid "a54e1fd7-9935-5657-bbe7-304f383e1956" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279144 1145 "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t),$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+4)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(4\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t))}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{sec}^{2}⁡(3t)}{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =4{sec}^{3}⁡(3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{9},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}{|}_{t=\\pi /9} & =4{sec}^{3}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{cos}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279146 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279147 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279148 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279149 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279150 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1041 "selection" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279149 13194139534154 true] [17592186279145 1110 #uuid "219a63ea-a8d7-5c77-98a4-568661cdc46c" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279146 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534154 true] [17592186279146 1111 #uuid "c0d4cd53-0fd9-5138-a845-0bd846cabd5d" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279147 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534154 true] [17592186279147 1103 #edb/ref 1759